[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218196701","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-3218196701","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":3218196701,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_0cjd","user":{"login":"DinoMC","id":9079110,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzkxMTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9079110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC","html_url":"https://github.com/DinoMC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T15:42:14Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T15:42:48Z","body":"Might be the Windows export version of #93106","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218196701/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218301240","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-3218301240","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":3218301240,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_02E4","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T18:50:56Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T18:50:56Z","body":"This is expected, per-monitor DPI awareness is not supported (will be implemented in 4.6), simply adding flag to manifest or changing `PROCESS_SYSTEM_DPI_AWARE` to `PROCESS_PER_MONITOR_DPI_AWARE` in the source will result in half broken behavior and not recommended.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218301240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218304285","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-3218304285","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":3218304285,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_020d","user":{"login":"DinoMC","id":9079110,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzkxMTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9079110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC","html_url":"https://github.com/DinoMC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T18:56:14Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T18:56:50Z","body":"@bruvzg I see, thanks! A bit off-topic then, but can you provide examples of broken behavior I should look out for, to make sure I'm not shipping my game in a broken state in the meantime?\n\n(With the default manifest, my game looks _fully_ broken if run on a monitor matching these conditions so this still sounds like the better option for me, from my limited testing)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218304285/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218309642","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-3218309642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":3218309642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_04IK","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T19:04:58Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T19:04:58Z","body":"> but can you provide examples of broken behavior I should look out for\n\nMostly issues with popup window positions/sizes and mouse input, if you are not using native windows in your game (`display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows` in the settings is set to true, which is default), it probably will work fine.\n\n> With the default manifest, my game looks fully broken if run on a monitor matching these conditions so this still sounds like the better option for me, from my limited testing\n\nWhat exactly is broken? With default manifest, it might be less sharp since window content is scaled by OS instead of rendering at native resolution, but should not have any other issues.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218309642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218312912","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-3218312912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":3218312912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_047Q","user":{"login":"DinoMC","id":9079110,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzkxMTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9079110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC","html_url":"https://github.com/DinoMC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T19:10:33Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T19:28:55Z","body":"Thanks! I hope it's ok then.\n\n> What exactly is broken? With default manifest, it might be less sharp since window content is scaled by OS instead of rendering at native resolution, but should not have any other issues.\n\nHere's an example. My game has a viewport of 640x360 with scale_mode set to \"integer\" :\n\n- Running my game with \"patched\" manifest : \n<img width=\"642\" height=\"392\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/483a298d-1d2f-4be1-baab-2c4ee64754b0\" />\n\n- Running it with default manifest : \n<img width=\"665\" height=\"417\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3c8bbfa-f5ef-4332-acf5-bf1cffd08582\" />\n\nEdit : It looks even blurrier on my screen, not sure why the screenshot is sharper.\n\nI don't have to do anything to end up with this, I just export, run the .exe, and it looks like that right away (but only if opened on a screen with different scaling from the main monitor).\n\nSame issue if I set it to fullscreen.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218312912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218320822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-3218320822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":3218320822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_0622","user":{"login":"DinoMC","id":9079110,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzkxMTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9079110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC","html_url":"https://github.com/DinoMC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DinoMC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T19:25:04Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T19:35:58Z","body":"Every single method of taking screenshots I try result in sharper images than the reality, very strange. So, for lack of a better solution, here's a photo of the difference between the screenshot and the running game. \nThe text is unreadable in game: \n\n<img width=\"1023\" height=\"373\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4882344-5b58-48ed-8526-6a16c09d48e8\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218320822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324071108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-6324071108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":6324071108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABePGqxA","user":{"login":"iansantagata","id":7070901,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzA5MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7070901?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata","html_url":"https://github.com/iansantagata","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iansantagata/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T18:58:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T19:20:33Z","body":"Chiming in here - I have this issue as well and have reproduced it in the editor using Godot v4.7.2 stable while working on my Windows 10 machine with different display scales.  For reference, my main monitor is a 1920 x 1200 with 125% scale and 2 side monitors each at 1920 x 1080 with 100% scale.  \n\nI stumbled across this issue after similarly seeing the suspicious 2400 x 1350 size returned from `DisplayServer.WindowGetSize()`, which, as @DinoMC reported, is exactly 1.25 times 1920 x 1080.\n\n@bruvzg - I see you mentioned above that the issue is per-monitor DPI awareness related and that functionality related to that would be implemented in Godot v4.6.  Is that still the case?  Curious if something got implemented to address this and I missed it or if I should be looking into alternative work-arounds.\n\nThanks in advance for assistance here!\n\nEdit - After posting this, I stumbled across this which is targeted for Godot 4.8 at the time I write this edit - https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2661.  Seems like this will at least allow the work-around of `DisplayServer.WindowGetSize()` to be usable on Windows, but I'm not sure if it will resolve the per-monitor DPI awareness that was referenced earlier in this issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324071108/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324247778","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-6324247778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":6324247778,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABePRc4g","user":{"login":"DigitalTableTops","id":169309929,"node_id":"U_kgDOChd26Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169309929?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops","html_url":"https://github.com/DigitalTableTops","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T19:07:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T19:07:22Z","body":"> 11\\. Chiming in here - I have this issue as well and have reproduced it in the editor using Godot v4.7.2 stable while working on my Windows 10 machine with different display scales.  For reference, my main monitor is a 1920 x 1200 with 125% scale and 2 side monitors each at 1920 x 1080 with 100% scale.\n>          I stumbled across this issue after similarly seeing the suspicious 2400 x 1350 size returned from `DisplayServer.WindowGetSize()`, which, as [@DinoMC](https://github.com/DinoMC) reported, is exactly 1.25 times 1920 x 1080.\n>          [@bruvzg](https://github.com/bruvzg) - I see you mentioned above that the issue is per-monitor DPI awareness related and that functionality related to that would be implemented in Godot v4.6.  Is that still the case?  Curious if something got implemented to address this and I missed it or if I should be looking into alternative work-arounds.\n>          Thanks in advance for assistance here!\n\nI do not believe it was fixed it 4.6. I have not noticed any changes.\n\nI have had great success patching my exe as described above with\n\n`<dpiAware xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2005/WindowsSettings\">true/pm</dpiAware>`\n\nI had catastrophic failure when also including the line\n\n`<ws2:dpiAwareness>PerMonitorV2</ws2:dpiAwareness>`\n\nThe former worked so well I am astonished that isn't the official default fix. I guess it messes up the plumbing somewhere, but I have had zero issues with and it fixed many problems all at once.\n\nThe latter broke a bunch of really important things, so I do not recommend it unless you are sure your project isn't effected.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324247778/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324328770","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-6324328770","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":6324328770,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABePWZQg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T19:11:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T19:11:33Z","body":"> Is that still the case?\n\nNo it is still not implemented.\n\n> I have had great success patching my exe as described above with\n\nSimply adding this (or changing `SetProcessDpiAwareness` in the code) will not fully fix it, it might work for some simple projects, but proper implementation will require a lot more changes to `Window` and `DisplayServer`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324328770/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324867768","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109932#issuecomment-6324867768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109932","id":6324867768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABeP3SuA","user":{"login":"DigitalTableTops","id":169309929,"node_id":"U_kgDOChd26Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169309929?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops","html_url":"https://github.com/DigitalTableTops","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DigitalTableTops/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T19:38:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T19:41:05Z","body":"You can assume my software is simple if you want, but it makes use of a large variety of DiplsayServer functions. I have not comes across a single issue that needed to be worked around when using the dpiAware tag. It fixed quite a few things with zero extra effort on my part. As I mentioned, the V2 tag broke many things all across the project and I strongly discourage using it.\n\nWhen using just the dpiAware tag, off the top of my head DisplayServer.screen_get_scale() returns the same wrong value as a non-patched exe but DisplayServer.screen_get_dpi() **does** return the correct value (so you can just calculate the scale from there). Not a big problem.\n\nCan you give some some specific examples of what to look out for? (EDIT: I have embed sub-windows disabled and it does not cause any problems at all. I think that might just be the V2 tag that does?)\n\nI think a great many projects, not just simple ones, would benefit from patching their exe's when they run into these sort of issues. I can understand why it's not the default (I phrased that poorly before) but I don't think it's productive to actively steer people aware from trying it when relevant.\n\nI'm just some random person on the internet though, so take that with a grain of salt. This thread comes up when searching for this problem on Google and such (along with tons of Reddit threads). This is the only place I see this fix mentioned and it does work rather well, IMO.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6324867768/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]